{
"i": 127,
"where": "スライド10",
"en": "When Does VS Use a Frame Pointer?",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 128,
"where": "スライド10",
"en": "[2] https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/prolog-and-epilog?view=msvc-160",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 129,
"where": "スライド10",
"en": "From [1] it definitely does if _alloca() is used",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 130,
"where": "スライド10",
"en": "\"_alloca is required to be 16-byte aligned and additionally required to use a frame pointer.\"",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 131,
"where": "スライド10",
"en": "\"If space is dynamically allocated (alloca) in a function, then a nonvolatile register must be used as a frame pointer to mark the base of the fixed part of the stack and that register must be saved and initialized in the prolog.\"",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 132,
"where": "スライド10",
"en": "Note it said \"a nonvolatile register\", it didn't say it had to be rbp. Elsewhere [2] they have an example using r13 instead of rbp",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 133,
"where": "スライド10",
"en": "Not clear if there are any other situations",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 135,
"where": "ノート10",
"en": "Colon notation means the full value is represented by the concatenation of the two values.",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 136,
"where": "ノート10",
"en": "If rdx = 0x11112222 and eax = 0x33334444, then rdx:eax is the quadword 0x1111222233334444",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 137,
"where": "ノート10",
"en": "http://2.bp.blogspot.com/-RA88gtJkvMM/UUYB6qSrLiI/AAAAAAAAADw/NU7nOMw8kCE/s1600/Eisntein5.jpg",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 140,
"where": "スライド11",
"en": "Still use frame pointers in the 32-bit style, unless directed not to by compile options",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 142,
"where": "スライド11",
"en": "First 6 parameters (from left to right) are put into RDI, RSI, RDX, RCX, R8, R9 respectively",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 143,
"where": "スライド11",
"en": "Remaining parameters “pushed” onto the stack so that the left-most parameter is at the lowest address",
"ja": ""
},
